<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. Robeson returns three months after starting treatment. He has taken sertraline 200 mg each morning for five weeks, after two weeks at 150 mg, without missing doses and with only mild loose stools. He has attended every weekly behavioral activation session; the psychologist reports PHQ-9 scores in the high teens at each session, with no positive item 9. He walks most days but still has little pleasure, wakes at four, and has not sung or accepted any invitations. He has had no thoughts of suicide. He has had no elation or reduced need for sleep. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Medicines</td><td>Sertraline 200 mg for five weeks after two weeks at 150 mg</td></tr><tr><td>Therapy</td><td>Eleven behavioral activation sessions</td></tr><tr><td>Mood</td><td>PHQ-9 17 from 22</td></tr><tr><td>Safety</td><td>No thoughts of suicide</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

