  <tr ID="problem-1">
    <td>About three months of low mood, exhaustion, poor sleep with waking at three in the morning, loss of interest in singing and reading, poor appetite with 5 kg weight loss, and withdrawal from friends, in a man of 58 under sustained political pressure; PHQ-9 22 with thoughts of being better off dead; depression suspected; medical causes being excluded and urgent psychiatric consultation arranged</td><td>resolved</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>R53.83</td><td>S — Synthetic presenting problem at intake, superseded by the diagnosis at the psychiatric consultation; anchored to his documented depression and loss of work (D).</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-2">
    <td>Major depressive disorder, recurrent, severe, without psychotic features (second episode; structured diagnostic interview; MDQ negative and no past hypomanic or manic episode on interview)</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>F33.2</td><td>S — Synthetic modern diagnosis anchored to his documented depression after the 1955 breakdown (D); the bipolar interpretation (R) is addressed and not adopted.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-3">
